Acknowledgments
---------------
Terraforming Mars is a board game designed by Jacob Fryxelius and published
by FryxGames (Stronghold Games and other partners publish localized
editions). Card names, card texts, milestone/award names and the Tharsis
map are the intellectual property of their rights holders. This project
contains no rulebook text, no card artwork and no game assets; it stores
only the structured card data an advisor needs (name, cost, tags,
requirements, effects) in cards/db.json and the hex layout in board.json.

The game engine is NOT part of this repository. The open-source
terraforming-mars app (https://github.com/terraforming-mars/terraforming-mars,
GPL-3.0) is fetched separately by scripts/vendor_bootstrap.sh into the
git-ignored vendor/ directory when a user wants the local training rig or
wants to regenerate the card data. cards/db.json and board.json ARE derived
from that engine's source (the exact commit is recorded in their "commit"
field, regenerated by scripts/extract_cards.py and scripts/extract_board.py);
because they are a derived work of a GPL-3.0 project, this repository is
published under the same licence.

The strategy knowledge base (strategy/) paraphrases publicly available
community analysis — no text is reproduced. Sources it is indebted to:
"A Quantified Guide to Terraforming Mars Strategy" (BoardGameGeek thread
1847708, I-Sheng Yang), boardgamestrategist.wordpress.com,
everythingisagame.com, boardoflife.wordpress.com, eriktwice.com, the Board
Game Arena forums and Steam community discussions, and BoardGameGeek thread
2388782 on starting hands. Their authors are not affiliated with this
project. Where the KB records measured prices from play, they come from
the project's own games.

